meta {
  name: List Households
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/households?page=1&pageSize=50
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  pageSize: 50
  ~q: rodriguez
  ~firstName: Jane
  ~lastName: Doe
  ~dateOfBirth: 1985-03-12
  ~householdRef: HH-2614
  ~policyNumber: AS-1234567
  ~status: Active
  ~sort: name
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

script:post-response {
  // Capture the first row's id for the other Households requests.
  // Runtime-only var (never persisted to disk).
  if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
    const items = res.getBody().items;
    if (items && items.length > 0) {
      bru.setVar("householdId", items[0].id);
    }
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns a paginated envelope", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("page");
    expect(body).to.have.property("pageSize");
    expect(body).to.have.property("total");
    expect(body).to.have.property("totalPages");
    expect(body).to.have.property("items");
    expect(body.items).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("rows expose only display fields (no internals leak)", function () {
    const items = res.getBody().items;
    if (items.length > 0) {
      const row = items[0];
      expect(row).to.have.property("name");
      expect(row).to.have.property("householdRef");
      expect(row).to.have.property("status");
      expect(row).to.have.property("totalActivePolicies");
      expect(row).to.have.property("matchedOn");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("legacySmartSuiteId");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("legacyAssignedCrmId");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("isTestRecord");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("agencyId");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("branchId");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("addressKey");
    }
  });

  test("an unfiltered list carries no match reason", function () {
    const items = res.getBody().items;
    if (items.length > 0) {
      expect(items[0].matchedOn).to.equal(null);
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /households

  The **Clients list** (`/clients`) — every household in the caller's scope, and
  the search that finds one from whichever identifier the caller is holding
  (PAC-89). Replaced the `{ status: 'ready' }` feature stub.

  - **Module:** `clients`
  - **Permission:** `clients:read` — **narrower than the rest of this
    controller.** `HouseholdRecordsController` carries a class-level OR-gate
    accepting `clients:read` **or** `crm_service:read`, because a household also
    renders inside a CRM ticket's drawer. This handler adds a handler-level
    `@RequirePermissions(clients:read)`; metadata override is per-key, so the
    two compose and the effective requirement is `clients:read`. A CSR holding
    only `crm_service:read` gets **403** here while `GET /households/:id` stays
    open to them.
  - **Data scope:** `own` collapses to **branch** — client records are shared
    and carry no per-user owner. Out-of-scope households are simply absent;
    existence never leaks across tenants.

  ## Query params
  | Param | Default | Notes |
  |---|---|---|
  | `page` | 1 | 1-based |
  | `pageSize` | 50 | max 100 |
  | `q` | — | Omni search, max 120 chars. Shape-routed; **ORs** across every dimension |
  | `firstName` | — | Contact first name, max 80 |
  | `lastName` | — | Contact last name, max 80 |
  | `dateOfBirth` | — | `YYYY-MM-DD`, contact DOB |
  | `householdRef` | — | `HH-2614`, `#HH2614` or the bare number |
  | `policyNumber` | — | Matched on the normalized key, so `AS 123-4567` finds `AS1234567` |
  | `status` | — | `Active` / `Inactive`. Repeated or comma-separated; ORed |
  | `sort` | `name` | `name` · `policies` · `updated` |

  The five explicit fields **AND** together (and with `q`); `q` alone ORs. The
  advanced panel is for a caller combining two identifiers; the omni box is for
  the common case of holding exactly one.

  ## How the search resolves
  Households are the result set, but three of the five identifiers live on
  **child** collections, so this runs in two phases rather than a `$lookup`:

  1. `contacts` (name, DOB) and `policies` (number) are queried under the same
     scope filter and resolved to household ids, each capped at 500 so one broad
     term cannot build an unbounded `$in`.
  2. Households are filtered by `$or` of `name`, `primaryContactName`,
     `householdRef` and those ids.

  `q` is routed by shape before it is used — `HH-\d+` to the reference, a parsed
  date (`YYYY-MM-DD` or `MM/DD/YYYY`) to date of birth, a normalized key of at
  least 4 alphanumerics to the policy number, and anything else to names.
  Routing is additive: a term that could be two things is queried as both.

  ## Response
  `{ page, pageSize, total, totalPages, items: HouseholdListRow[] }` — the same
  envelope as `GET /leads`.

  Each row is a `HouseholdSummary` plus `householdRef`, `primaryEmail`,
  `primaryPhone`, `city`, `state`, `assignedCrmId`, `updatedAt`, and:

  - **`matchedOn`** — `{ field, value }` or `null`. Why the row is in the
    results, set **only** for a reason the row cannot already show: `member`,
    `dateOfBirth` or `policy`. A household matched on its own name or reference
    leaves it null, because both are printed in the row's first column.
    Searching a policy number otherwise returns households whose names match
    nothing the caller typed, and the list reads as broken.

  `city`/`state` come from `resolveHouseholdAddress`, which coerces the three
  writers' differing key shapes (`street` / `line1` / `location_address`) into
  one — never read `propertyAddress` raw.

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 400 | `dateOfBirth` not `YYYY-MM-DD`, `page`/`pageSize` out of bounds, `status` outside the vocabulary, unknown `sort` |
  | 401 | Missing/expired bearer token |
  | 403 | `clients` disabled for the agency, or the caller lacks `clients:read` (a CSR with only `crm_service:read` lands here) |

  A `householdRef` or `policyNumber` that cannot be a reference or a key at all
  returns an **empty page**, not the unfiltered book — a search that silently
  widens is the failure this guards against.
}
